> belief.  However desirable this may be, you could choose to
> do otherwise and believe any old thing. Many people do.

Although both I and Anton are capable of freely choosing
to ignore evidence, if we choose to pay attention to
evidence, which we do so choose, we are not capable of
choosing to believe any old thing.

In addition if we choose to ignore evidence that we know is
relevant, we are conscious of choosing wrongly, and cannot
choose to believe otherwise.

Our wills are free, but if we freely choose to walk over a
cliff, there will be a great deal of internal resistance,
as is demonstrated in bungee jumping.

Yet nonetheless we, and everyone else, is free to walk
over a cliff if they so choose.

